==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|invelop}}, {{l|en|invelope}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{l|en|envelope}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} BLUE BLUE BLUE CHEESE !!!!!!!!!!!!!" from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|wrappan-|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|wlappan-||to wrap, roll up, turn, wind|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|werb-||to turn, bend|lang=ine-pro}} [http://www.wordnik.com/words/envelop]. Akin to {{etyl|enm|-}} {{term|wlappen||to wrap, fold|lang=enm}} (Modern English ''[[lap]]'' "to wrap, involve, fold"), Middle English {{term|wrappen||to wrap|lang=enm}}, {{dum}} {{term|lappen||to wrap up, embrace|lang=dum}}, {{etyl|da|-}} dialectal ''[[vravle]]'' "to wind, twist", {{etyl|gml|-}} ''[[wrempen]]'' "to wrinkle, distort", Old English {{term|wearp||warp|lang=ang}}. More at [[in]], [[wrap]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ĕn-vĕl'əp}}, {{IPA|/ɛnˈvɛləp/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/En"vEl@p/}}
* {{audio|en-us-envelop.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en-uk-envelop.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

